ding proofs and their age relative to the specified H hours.\n\nThe current implementation checks for missing proofs and validates the writer's ranges. I'll need to modify the logic to track pending timestamp proofs and compare their age against the threshold.\n\nWhen a proof is pending, we should calculate its age by subtracting the Sigstore attestation time from the current time. If this exceeds H hours, we should mark the proof as too old and potentially fail the verification.\n\nThe solution requires adding a new argument to the check-anchors command that allows specifying the maximum allowed pending time, with a default behavior of accepting all pending proofs.","thinking_blocks":[],"action":{"command":"cd /workspace && git log --oneline -5","is_input":false,"reset":false,"kind":"TerminalAction"},"tool_name":"terminal","tool_call_id":"terminal_4mp71xx0d6dg","tool_call":{"id":"terminal_4mp71xx0d6dg","name":"terminal","arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace && git log --oneline -5\"}","origin":"completion"},"llm_response_id":"gen-1794385434-vIeLNu9LxSb9AYHWTmwl","security_risk":"UNKNOWN","summary":"terminal: {\"command\": \"cd /workspace && git log --oneline -5\"}","kind":"ActionEvent"}
