+{"id":"82d94903-751a-403e-92a3-6263eb3b06f5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:24:35.726130","source":"agent","parent_id":"8cda0b13-3883-43fb-93f2-825cb6d7849e","thought":[],"reasoning_content":"Based on my reading of the code and requirements, I need to implement the `--max-pending-hours H` option for the `check-anchors` command in `record/record.py`. The current implementation shows that:\n\n1. `check_ots()` function returns `None` when a proof is pending (line 376)\n2. `iso(t)` function (line 379-381) returns `None` if the timestamp is pending\n3. The `check-anchors` command currently accepts pending proofs and exits with 0\n\nThe requirements are:\n- Without the option, behaviour is unchanged (pending proofs accepted, exit 0)\n- With the option, if any range head's proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago, exit 1 and print to stderr a message containing `still pending N h`\n- A pending proof younger than H hours is fine (exit 0)\n- All existing tests must still pass\n\nLet me analyze the code structure more carefully to understand what needs to be changed:\n\n1. Add `--max-pending-hours H` argument to the parser\n2. Modify `cmd_check_anchors` to check for pending proofs and compare their age against H\n3. The pending proof's age is based on when it was created (Sigstore attestation time)\n4. If a proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation is older than H hours, it should fail\n\nLooking at the code:\n- In `cmd_check_anchors()`, for each anchor:\n  - For `.sigstore.json` files: we get `t` (timestamp) and `pred` (predicate)\n  - For `.ots` files: we get `t` which is `None` when pending\n- The issue mentions \"range head's proof is still pending and its Sigstore attestation time is more than H hours ago\"\n- So we need to look at `.sigstore.json` anchors, and if the corresponding `.ots` file is missing/pending, check how old the Sigstore attestation is\n\nLet me implement this step by step:","thinking_blocks":[],"action":{"command":"