+{"id":"bfa06c78-b026-474b-bfa5-0ccb3c3c6577","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:25:16.643634","source":"agent","parent_id":"a483f65a-baf3-4502-bd12-dc426473a158","thought":[],"reasoning_content":"The argument `--max-pending-hours` is already added to the parser. So the parser part is correct.\n\nNow let's look at the actual `cmd_check_anchors` function and modify it to:\n- When `a.max_pending_hours` is provided (not None), we should:\n   - For each range head, check the pending status\n   - If a proof is pending and its Sigstore attestation time is older than H hours, exit 1\n   - Print to stderr a message containing `still pending N h`\n\nFor the actual implementation details:\n- The `check_ots` function returns `None` if pending\n- The `check_sigstore` function returns `t` (timestamp) for sigstore anchors\n- For OTS anchors (the `.ots` files), they should correspond to the range head\n- For Sigstore anchors (`.sigstore.json`), they correspond to a range head and have an attestation time `t`\n- The pending check is: when `check_ots` returns `None`\n- The Sigstore attestation time is the timestamp from the bundle: `int(json.loads(raw)[\"verificationMaterial\"][\"tlogEntries\"][0][\"integratedTime\"])`\n\nWe need to:\n1. Keep a mapping of which range heads are attested by Sigstore (those that are `.sigstore.json` anchors)\n2. For each such head, check:\n   - If its corresponding `.ots` file is present and is not pending\n   - If the `.ots` file is pending AND the Sigstore attestation time is older than `H` hours, report an error and exit 1\n   - If the `.ots` file is not pending, that's okay (exit 0) even if Sigstore is old\n   - If the `.ots` file is present and confirmed, that's okay\n\nWait, looking at the code: The `.ots` anchor file is the OpenTimestamps proof of the entry NNNN's bytes\nThe `.sigstore.json` anchor is the Sigstore attestation of the range of entries it added, ending at NNNNNN\n\nThe code already:\n- Collects `stamped` as range heads that have an `.ots` file\n- Checks that every range head (`.sigstore.json`) has its corresponding `.ots` file (`if hi not in stamped: bad.append(...)`)\n\nSo for the max-pending-hours requirement, we need to:\n1. For each range head (signature: `.sigstore.json` anchors), get its attestation time `t`\n2. Check if it has an OTS proof (i.eレビュ containing `check_ots` logic above)\n\n\n3. If OTS proof is pending (`check_ots` returns `None`), then compute the age of the Sigstore attestation\n4. If age > `H` hours, report and exit 1\n5. Otherwise, if age <= `H` hours, it's okay (exit 0)\n\nI'll proceed with a detailed implementation approach for the check function.\n\nWe'll modify the existing anchor verification logic to track Sigstore attestation times and compare them against the OpenTimestamps proof status. The key is to introduce a precise time-based validation that checks pending proofs against a specified time threshold.\n\nWe'll need to carefully track the attestation age, ensuring we capture both the timestamp and the pending state of the OTS proof. This requires careful parsing of the anchor files and precise time calculations.\n\nThe implementation will involve three main checks: verifying all range heads have corresponding OTS proofs, checking pending proof ages, and ensuring the latest timestamp matches the last range head.\n\nI'll need to track the Sigstore attestation times, extract them, and calculate elapsed hours for pending OTS proofs. The key challenge is finding the attestation time for a Sigstore anchor, which comes from the `integratedTime` field in the bundle. When an OTS proof is pending, we'll need to compute its age by comparing the Sigstore attestation timestamp with the current time. This requires careful time comparison and conversion.\n\nI'll track the Sigstore timestamps, check for pending OTS proofs, and generate appropriate warning messages for proofs that exceed the specified hours. The goal is to provide precise warnings while maintaining the existing test suite's integrity.","thinking_blocks":[],"tool_name":"file_editor","tool_call_id":"file_editor_22fz67nq83k1","tool_call":{"id":"file_editor_22fz67nq83k1","name":"file_editor","arguments":"{\"_openhands_malformed_tool_call\": true, \"error\": \"Error validating tool 'file_editor': Invalid \\\\escape: line 1 column 2248 (char 2247). Arguments: unparseable JSON\"}","origin":"completion"},"llm_response_id":"gen-1794385497-9yqvbzFhOGuibsSsrwZl","security_risk":"UNKNOWN","kind":"ActionEvent"}
